{
  "info": {
    "name": "Oculus API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "SIEM with honeypot-based insider-threat detection.\n\n**Try it:** call `POST /api/login`, copy the `token` from the response, press **Authorize** and paste it. Seeded demo accounts are listed in the README (`imran.shah@oculus.com` is an analyst).\n\n**Auth:** a JWT, as a Bearer token or an httpOnly cookie. Cookie writes also need an `X-CSRF-Token` header equal to the `oculus_csrf` cookie; Bearer clients do not.\n\n**Errors:** always `{\"success\": false, \"message\": \"...\"}`."
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "description": "",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Sign in as analyst",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Signed in\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"Response carries a token\", () => pm.expect(body.token).to.be.a(\"string\"));",
                  "pm.environment.set(\"token\", body.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "Run this first for the Console and Admin folders. Saves the JWT to {{token}}.",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{adminUser}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Sign in as employee",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Signed in\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"Response carries a token\", () => pm.expect(body.token).to.be.a(\"string\"));",
                  "pm.environment.set(\"token\", body.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "Run this first for the Workspace folder. Saves the JWT to {{token}}.",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{employeeUser}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{employeePassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Sign in (custom body)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "description": "Returns a JWT and sets two cookies: `oculus_token` (httpOnly, SameSite=Strict) and `oculus_csrf`. API clients can ignore the cookies and send `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (no CSRF header needed). Five failures from one address for one account, or 20 from one address in 15 minutes, lock that address out (429).",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "login"
              ],
              "query": []
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"imran.shah@oculus.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Oculus#Admin26\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Signed in\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"Response carries a token\", () => pm.expect(body.token).to.be.a(\"string\"));",
                  "pm.environment.set(\"token\", body.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
